ItemTooltip: {
	AmuletOfGlory:
		'''
		Hitting enemies increases your movement and mining speed
		Enemies nearby chests will emit light
		'''
	CrystalStompers: Double-Tap Down to perform a crystal stomp
	OpalOfCaVea:
		'''
		Glowing crystals grow on your back every 5 seconds, up to 3
		Enemies take damage if all 3 crystals have spawned
		'''
	PlatinumHook: Extends all gem hooks and upgrades them to glow
	LargeGeode:
		'''
		Not consumable
		Summons the Crystal Tumbler
		Only usable in the Caverns Arena
		'''
	ObsidianEye:
		'''
		Not consumable
		Summons Cyvercry
		Only usable at night
		'''
	OnTheRocks: "'Stone-Aged'"
	ResonanceDrill: Mines connected ore, the more you mine the more effective
	ElectricBlueSolution: Spreads Crystal Caverns
	SpeedstersPickaxe: Mining ramps up the speed of your pickaxe
	DeepFreeze: "'Is it cold in here, or is it just me?'"
	ElementalShift:
		'''
		Attacking creates an energy ball that can be hit around
		Right-Click to destroy the ball
		'''
	Eos:
		'''
		Ends a combo with a spin attack
		Hit enemies with the spin while dashing to bash off of them, gaining brief invulnerability
		After bashing an enemy, your next 2 combos will fire projectiles
		'''
	ExtinguishedDynamite: ""
	CrystalCrescent: Throws out a returning quarterstaff after a rapid swing
	NerveFlagellator:
		'''
		Attacks with multiple nerve tendrils
		Marked enemies may spawn a friendly nerve creeper when hit
		'''
	BurningJealousy:
		'''
		Hold Right-Click to guard, gaining a large defense boost
		Retaliate with an explosive counter-attack if hit while guarding
		'''
	Solsear:
		'''
		Fires a continuous laser that deals more damage at the tip
		Right-Click to fire a bomb
		Aim the tip of the laser into the bomb to increase its damage and size
		'With great firepower comes great irresponsibility'
		'''
	FlareGun:
		'''
		Does not require ammo
		5% summon tag crit chance
		Click again with good timing to fire faster
		'''
	CerobaStaffItem:
		'''
		Right-Click to attack with a ward that marks enemies
		Marked enemies take massively increased damage from the weapon
		'''
	ClockworkLazinator:
		'''
		Right-Click to wind up the weapon, increasing how long it fires for
		Caps out at 4 winds
		'''
	CrystalGlade: Right-Click to summon a portal that will change where your shots originate from
	TheBeacon:
		'''
		Targets the closest enemy to the mouse
		Releases flaming tendrils around the targeted enemy
		'''
	TheFlashlight: Targets the closest enemy to the mouse
	TheLaserPointer:
		'''
		Targets the closest enemy to the mouse
		Releases homing sparks after locking onto the same enemy for a while
		'''
	WandOfExploding: Inflicts Mana Burn, causing enemies to leak stars that restore mana
	TetraBlades: Right-Click to dash up to 4 times
	TheSahara:
		'''
		Hold to charge, increasing damage and velocity
		Releases a fire vortex at full charge
		'''
	WarBow:
		'''
		Hold to charge, increasing damage and velocity
		Embeds a spike into enemies at full charge
		'''
	GraniteCannon:
		'''
		Converts bullets into granite chunks
		If two chunks collide midair, they break into homing energy cores
		'''
	AdamantitePulsar:
		'''
		Does not require ammo
		Right-Click to change modes
		'''
	RedundantFibber:
		'''
		+50% love
		'Would I lie to you?'
		Bullets shot will ricochet
		'''
	ShotgunAxe:
		'''
		Converts bullets into a special projectile
		Right-Click to chop with the axe, gouging enemies
		'''
	Skylight:
		'''
		Does not require ammo
		Right-Click to summon a massive lightning bolt from the sky
		'''
	TheInfinity:
		'''
		'It's closer than you think! (No it isn't)'
		Right-Click to change elements
		'''
	MarbleMusket:
		'''
		Converts bullets into special gravity-affected projectiles
		Hitting 3 consecutive shots releases homing stars
		'''
	PouchOfRocks: Throws 2 magnetic stones which can collide and explode
	TitaniumRocketLauncher:
		'''
		Does not require ammo
		Right-Click to shoot a large rocket that follows the mouse
		'''
	H2OCaliber: Fires bubbles which can merge
	OceanMist: Casts a water burst
	MeteorCrossbow: Fires a rocket arrow
	PoundOfFeathers: "'Weighs less than a pound of bricks!'"
	LightOfTheAncients:
		'''
		Fires small, fast hellfire bullets
		Has a visible overheating gauge above the player that fills as you fire
		The gun becomes more powerful as it heats up, but if you keep firing it will need to cool down
		'''
	Marionette:
		'''
		Continuously drain mana to summon a set of handle bars and puppet strings at the cursor.
		The ends of the strings can attach to enemies and choke their arteries.
		If the handle bars get too far from a string's attach point, or if a string stays attached for too long, it will weaken and snap.
		Choke damage gains a small crit chance for every string that is attached.
		'''
	BishopsStaff:
		'''
		Hold [Attack(Left Click)] to ground the staff and channel mana towards it
		While channeling, the staff generates a starry sky above itself
		The stars fire stellar beams towards the ground and generate faster over time
		After some time, larger stars will generate, firing larger beams
		'''
	PhanticWhip:
		'''
		Inflicts enemies with a short-timed soul sapping effect
		Your minions capture soul energy from afflicted enemies
		The energy is released when you next swing the whip in an arc of spirits
		'''
	RedShade:
		'''
		Projectiles home in and possess enemies
		Possessed enemies release smaller copies of the spirit upon death
		'''
	Soulerang: This boomerang has a unique flight pattern, and can go through blocks
	Specter:
		'''
		Left click to stab forward
		Right click to slash and wound enemies for a short time
		'''
	BandOfCrystallization:
		'''
		Grows 1 defense every 10 seconds in combat, up to 10
		Outside combat, grows 1 defense every 5 seconds, up to 20
		Entering combat sheds defense above 10; bosses keep you in combat
		Glowing crystals show your growing protection
		Removing the band sheds its crystals
		'''
	PetrifiedShackles:
		'''
		Grants 1 defense and reduces attack speed by 10%
		Grows 1 defense every 7 seconds in combat, up to 15
		Outside combat, grows 1 defense every 4 seconds, up to 25
		Entering combat sheds growth above 15; bosses keep you in combat
		Cannot be equipped with Band of Crystallization
		'''
	SpikesInABottle:
		'''
		Allows a Cloud-strength double jump that scatters crystal caltrops
		Taking at least 15% of maximum life in one hit scatters more after half a second
		The retaliation can occur once every 6 seconds
		Cannot be made into a balloon: it would pop
		'''
	CrystalDrillrow:
		'''
		Drills through one continuous section of terrain, up to 12 tiles thick
		Emerges with an energized crystal tip that deals 15% more damage
		The worn drill breaks against the next wall
		'''
	CrystalStoneSlug:
		'''
		Embeds crystal splinters for 3 seconds on impact
		Well-timed throws deal 2x Skill Strike damage
		'''
	StoneSlug:
		'''
		A heavy sling stone with a steep, short-range arc
		Well-timed throws deal 2.25x Skill Strike damage
		'''
	WoodSlug:
		'''
		A light sling slug with a long, shallow arc
		Well-timed throws deal 1.5x Skill Strike damage
		'''
	TumblingHarness:
		'''
		Summons a rideable tumblerock
		Hold Up while grounded to conjure an electric ramp; keep holding to loop
		Release Up to leap off along the ramp's direction
		Electrifies the ball while ramp riding and briefly after launching, dealing contact damage
		Negates fall damage while mounted
		'''
	Minerall:
		'''
		Increases mining speed by 15%, movement speed by 10%, and mining reach by 1
		Lasts 5 minutes and stacks with Mining Potion
		'''
	MineralWater:
		'''
		Restores 60 life with 30 seconds of potion sickness
		Grants 40 defense for 30 seconds, but inflicts mineral poisoning for 12 seconds
		Poisoning drains 10 life per second
		Contains enough sediment to cause stomach or throat stones. Worse than a kidney stone.
		'''
	BabyCondurtleEgg:
		'''
		Hatches a Baby Condurtle town pet
		Permanently welcomes it to this world; it can share a home with a townsperson
		Occasionally laid by living Condurtles
		'''
	GlimmerwoodHamaxe: ""
	CrystalTumblerBag:
		'''
		Right click to open
		Contains a Tumbler weapon and the Tumbling Harness
		'''
	ConductorWand:
		'''
		Channel a tethered electric bubble that gathers your minions
		Three captured minions and an additional 50 mana unleash a single plasma shock
		Drains 2 mana plus 2 per captured summon every half second
		Release to free your summons; start a new bubble to shock again
		Alternatively carries one sentry; falling sentries release a landing shock
		'''
	FenceSitter:
		'''
		Each swing strikes one enemy with a weighty stop
		Land four consecutive swings to unleash four lightning fences on the fifth
		Each fence stops at terrain and strikes each enemy twice
		Missing or changing weapons breaks the streak
		'''
	Geomagnetic:
		'''
		Fires a crackling beam of geomagnetic lightning
		At or below 25% mana, casts a hovering sphere that releases three bolts
		The sphere electrifies enemies on contact
		'''
	TumblerAccelerator:
		'''
		Catapults tiny tumblers without ammunition
		Right click to suspend airborne tumblers, charge them, and launch them toward your cursor
		Paired impacts electrify enemies
		'''
	BluntJavelin: A heavy cavern-stone javelin that breaks apart on impact
	CavernousRampart:
		'''
		Hold to guard toward the cursor; cannot be used while mounted
		Hits against the shield receive 12 additional defense
		A guarded hit exceeding 20% of maximum life shatters it for 6 seconds
		Fast movement bashes enemies and grants a brief moment of invulnerability
		'''
	CavernsBrandistock:
		'''
		Successful thrusts build blade stress
		At 40% stress, three hidden crystal blades extend and Skill Strike
		At maximum stress, the blades shatter and retract for 4 seconds
		You can still thrust in staff mode while the mechanism recovers
		Pause between attacks to let the stress fall
		'''
	Faultbreaker: A weighty sledgehammer with a crushing overhead swing
	GlimmerwoodBow:
		'''
		Every third shot turns its arrow into a Crystal Drillrow
		Drillrows bore through one section of terrain
		'''
	GlimmerwoodSword: A simple wooden blade with a glimmer in its grain
	PinCushionStone:
		'''
		First throw launches a floating pin-cushion stone
		Further throws fire darts that pierce one enemy
		Darts lodge in the stone and nudge it, empowering its next impacts
		Every third empowered collision rebounds much harder
		After 10 seconds without a dart, the stone dissolves and releases its pins
		'''
	RockRumbler:
		'''
		Shoulder-fpires rocky energy bombs that shatter in a crystal blast
		The white-hot launch burst marks the direct-hit Skill Strike window
		Bombs lose their thrust and drop heavily after the burst
		Does not consume ammo
		'''
	Saphead:
		'''
		Channel to spiral a living sapper head around you
		Move the cursor closer to tighten its orbit and spout crystal fog faster
		The stem glows and the flower swells before each puff
		Consumes 5 mana per puff; the initial cast pays for the first
		Release to coil the stem back into your hand
		'A severed sapper stem, improbably still alive'
		'''
	SaplingCane:
		'''
		Plants three baby sappers using one sentry slot
		Hold right click to guide them in short hops and designate enemies
		They snap at nearby foes and return to their patch when left alone
		Bites against your designated summon target deal Skill Strikes
		'''
	Shattershot:
		'''
		Blasts four heavy pieces of flint and gravel in a wide spread
		Consumes one stone block or cavern stone per blast
		Cavern stone fires glowing gravel and sometimes an extra white-hot crystal fragment
		'''
	SpeleothemConjurer:
		'''
		Channel a stationary shower of ethereal stalactites at the cursor
		Consumes 6 mana per spike; impacts leave crystal sediment
		Release to pull the sediment together and erupt a towering stalagmite
		Gather 12 impacts for a Skill Strike; the crystal shines white when ready
		'''
	StackerRock:
		'''
		Rocks meant for stacking
		Thrown discs anchor to solid floors and can be stacked from above
		Each added rock extends the tower’s lifetime
		Hit a tower from the side to topple it early
		'''
	TheSling:
		'''
		Hold to wind up a slug in a moth-silk sling
		Release to throw in the direction the pouch is traveling
		Aim beyond the orbit; the white flash and chime mark a powerful, well-aligned throw
		Stone slugs hit hard, wood flies farther, and crystal leaves splinters
		Uses one slug per wind-up
		'''
	TumblerCommander:
		'''
		Channel to guide a tiny tumbler along floors and walls toward the cursor
		More distant targets make it roll faster
		Consumes 4 mana each half-second
		'''
	TungstenCluster:
		'''
		An unusually pure ore specimen
		Turn in to the Rock Collector for 65 silver coins and 5 cavern crystals
		Hold the specimen to choose it; favorite it to keep it
		'''
	TitaniumSuperCluster:
		'''
		An unusually pure ore specimen
		Turn in to the Rock Collector for 520 silver coins and 12 cavern crystals
		Hold the specimen to choose it; favorite it to keep it
		'''
	TitaniumCluster:
		'''
